    {
      "id": 20,
      "definition": {
        "type": "note",
        "content": "## ClickHouse data-plane health (#183)\n\nThese tiles distinguish \"click-dog is down\" (entire row blank — no scrape) from \"click-dog is up but ClickHouse is not emitting useful data\" (tiles populated but red). Pair the **newest span age** tile with the cockpit's **last success age**: when last-success is fresh but newest-span-age keeps climbing, click-dog is polling ClickHouse but `system.opentelemetry_span_log` has gone quiet. The **enrichment failure** rate isolates query_log join health independent of span flow. **Spans with query_id** below 1.0 is the signal Datadog query-analysis dashboards lose context — confirm the OpenTelemetry trace propagation in your ClickHouse client.",
        "background_color": "gray",
        "font_size": "14",
        "text_align": "left",
        "show_tick": false,
        "has_padding": true
      },
      "layout": {"x": 0, "y": 23, "width": 12, "height": 1}
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "definition": {
        "type": "query_value",
        "title": "Newest span_log row age",
