    {
      "id": 28,
      "definition": {
        "type": "note",
        "content": "## Topology self-audit\n\nDetects the **sidecar + `use_cluster_queries` anti-pattern**: more than one click-dog instance running whole-cluster span reads → N× duplicate exports and cluster-wide query load. `0` (green) = one reader doing cluster-wide reads (or none); `1` (red) = duplicate cluster-wide reads detected. The `reason` tag splits **`sidecar_cluster_queries`** (per-node sidecars each going cluster-wide — turn `use_cluster_queries` off) from **`multi_instance_cluster_queries`** (separate readers not sharing a Keeper election — run a single cluster-mode reader, or 2–3 sharing one election). The **Per-host health** table's *topology warning* column shows which nodes trip.\n\nThis signal is **indirect**: a **grey / no-data** tile is **not** healthy — it means OTLP self-metrics are not being exported (or, on the legacy scrape path, the metric is not being scraped or the OpenMetrics rename is missing). It is observability-only: detection never affects `/readyz` or de-rotates a node. First detection lands roughly `interval_s × debounce_count` (~10 min at defaults) after the misconfig appears.\n\nA red tile can also reflect **legitimate, bounded** duplication — a sustained Keeper outage (instances fail open and export by design) or a long-running backfill from another host — and clears on its own once resolved.",
        "background_color": "gray",
        "font_size": "14",
        "text_align": "left",
        "show_tick": false,
        "has_padding": true
      },
      "layout": {"x": 2, "y": 28, "width": 10, "height": 2}
    }
  ]
